* Lab 06-04 -- static IR drop in small power grids (Example 06-04.5 and Problem 06-04.10).
* Each grid is a mesh of equal resistors; every node draws a constant current (a current
* source from the node to ground) and supply bumps are ideal voltage sources.
*
* EXPECT ex5vmin  key:../../chapters/06-04-nodal-analysis.md#Ex_06-04.5c rtol=1e-4
* EXPECT ex5drop  key:../../chapters/06-04-nodal-analysis.md#Ex_06-04.5d scale=1e-3 rtol=2e-3
* EXPECT ex5ibump key:../../chapters/06-04-nodal-analysis.md#Ex_06-04.5e rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT p10a     key:../../solutions/06-04-solutions.md#06-04.10c scale=1e-3 rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT p10b     key:../../solutions/06-04-solutions.md#06-04.10d scale=1e-3 rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT p10c     key:../../solutions/06-04-solutions.md#06-04.10e scale=1e-3 rtol=1e-6

* ---- g5: 5 x 5 nodes, 10 mOhm per edge, 0.5 A per node, bumps at [(0, 0), (0, 4), (4, 0), (4, 4)]
Rg5h00 g5_00 g5_01 0.01
Rg5v00 g5_00 g5_10 0.01
